<article class="env-exercise" id="03FM">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03FM">Exercise <span data-tag="03FM">7.6.2.5</span>.</a> Let $G$ be a group and let $H \subseteq G$ be a commutative normal subgroup, so that we have a commutative diagram of Kan complexes </p>
<div class="equation" id="03FN">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="03FN" href="/tag/03FN">7.71</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:exact-sequence-pullback-square} \xymatrix@C =50pt@R=50pt{ B_{\bullet }H \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  B_{\bullet } G \ar [d] \\ \Delta ^0 \ar [r] &amp;  B_{\bullet }(G/H) } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
Show that (<a data-tag="03FN" href="/tag/03FN">7.71</a>) is a pullback diagram in the ordinary category of Kan complexes, and that it determines a pullback diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}= \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}(\operatorname{Kan})$ (see Example <a data-tag="03G5" href="/tag/03G5">7.6.3.2</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show that, if $H$ is contained in the center of $G$, then the diagram (<a data-tag="03FN" href="/tag/03FN">7.71</a>) is also pullback square in the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show that, if $H$ is not contained in the center of $G$, then the diagram $B_{\bullet } G \rightarrow B_{\bullet } (G/H) \leftarrow \Delta ^0$ does not have a limit in the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$. In particular, the diagram (<a data-tag="03FN" href="/tag/03FN">7.71</a>) is not a pullback square in $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
